cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these exercises or their fixtures in a course, a paper or a syllabus, please cite them as below."
title: "Tennis API exercises: graded coding exercises for a real JSON API"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-23"
authors:
  - name: "Live Tennis API"
    website: "https://livetennisapi.com"
    email: "hello@livetennisapi.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/livetennisapi/tennis-api-exercises"
url: "https://github.com/livetennisapi/tennis-api-exercises"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Eight graded exercises in Python and JavaScript that teach students to work
  with a real JSON API. Students handle nested data, errors, rate limits and a
  daily request quota. Tests run offline against API responses from Live Tennis
  API, most recorded live and a few built from its specification. Code is MIT.
  Fixtures are CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - teaching
  - programming exercises
  - REST API
  - JSON
  - Python
  - JavaScript
  - tennis
  - sports data
